Author: Andrew Scott <atscott@google.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 11 09:00:32 2024 -0700

Remove deprecation on Router guard interfaces (#56408) Many developers find these interfaces useful for various reasons. Beyond that, the deprecation of the interfaces has incorrectly implied that existing class-based guard implementations need to be migrated to functions. Class injectables are _not_ deprecated and choosing to implement a guard's state and logic as a class that is injectable in the functions run inside the injection context is valid. resolves #50234 PR Close #56408



